::ALG1_U02_L01_Quiz_Q13::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L01_Q13<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>No new primary MLA standard; prerequisite support.<br><br>Question:<br>Which operation solves z + 10 = 24? {
=A. Subtract 10 from both sides#Correct. Subtraction undoes addition.
~B. Add 10 to both sides#This repeats the operation instead of undoing it.
~C. Divide both sides by 10#Division does not undo addition.
~D. Multiply both sides by 10#Multiplication does not undo addition.
}

::ALG1_U02_L01_Quiz_Q14::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L01_Q14<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>No new primary MLA standard; prerequisite support.<br><br>Question:<br>Which operation solves h - 12 = 6? {
~A. Subtract 12 from both sides#This repeats the subtraction instead of undoing it.
=B. Add 12 to both sides#Correct. Addition undoes subtraction.
~C. Divide both sides by 12#Division does not undo subtraction.
~D. Multiply both sides by 12#Multiplication does not undo subtraction.
}

::ALG1_U02_L01_Quiz_Q15::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L01_Q15<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>No new primary MLA standard; prerequisite support.<br><br>Question:<br>Which operation solves 8g = 56? {
~A. Subtract 8 from both sides#Subtraction does not undo multiplication by 8.
~B. Add 8 to both sides#Addition does not undo multiplication by 8.
=C. Divide both sides by 8#Correct. Division undoes multiplication.
~D. Multiply both sides by 8#This repeats multiplication instead of undoing it.
}

::ALG1_U02_L01_Quiz_Q16::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L01_Q16<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>No new primary MLA standard; prerequisite support.<br><br>Question:<br>Which operation solves <sup>j</sup>&frasl;<sub>6</sub> = 3? {
~A. Subtract 6 from both sides#Subtraction does not undo division by 6.
~B. Add 6 to both sides#Addition does not undo division by 6.
~C. Divide both sides by 6#This repeats the division instead of undoing it.
=D. Multiply both sides by 6#Correct. Multiplication undoes division.
}

::ALG1_U02_L01_Quiz_Q17::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L01_Q17<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>No new primary MLA standard; prerequisite support.<br><br>Question:<br>Which value checks correctly for x + 3 = 10? {
=A. x = 7#Correct. 7 + 3 = 10.
~B. x = 13#13 + 3 is 16, not 10.
~C. x = 3#3 + 3 is 6, not 10.
~D. x = 10#10 + 3 is 13, not 10.
}

::ALG1_U02_L01_Quiz_Q18::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L01_Q18<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>No new primary MLA standard; prerequisite support.<br><br>Question:<br>Which value checks correctly for y - 4 = 11? {
